---
Scope: confirmed production accessibility behavior in final DI1–6 integration, explicitly authorized by lead before author test/evidence freeze. This verdict does NOT assess, accept, or invent failures in unfinished DI5 tests, browser integration scripts or final manifest. Production remains accepted DI4.2 plus accepted DI6. Lead has conceded F1. No fixes, production edits, git changes, ledger edits, gates or deployment performed by checker.

FAILURE F1 — focused Dashboard detail controls completely hidden by automatic refresh notice
Constitution point 9; WCAG 2.2 AA 2.4.11 Focus Not Obscured (Minimum), also invisible focus indicator under 2.4.7. A keyboard user edits the From date; a refresh revision causes the production dirty-edit notice to appear. Normal Tab navigation subsequently focuses detail controls entirely behind that opaque fixed notice. They remain focused and operable but neither the component nor its focus indicator is visible. Reproduces with ALL application scripts active, not merely the worker's script-stripped refresh harness.

Production locations: web/static/js/page-refresh.js:39 creates fixed bottom-4/right-4/left-6/z-50 notice; :72 appends it without preventing coverage of newly focused content. Affected DI3 controls in web/templates/components/kpis.html:12 Income details, :24 Cash-flow details, :41 Budget details, :72 Healthcare details.

Observed rectangles in both light and dark, viewport height 900 (x,y,width,height; CSS px):
390 Income details: component (33,852,96.5625,20), notice (24,738,350,146), scrollY=0.
390 Budget details: component (33,763,94.90625,20), notice (24,738,350,146), scrollY=563.
768 Cash-flow details: component (33,847,111.1875,20), notice (24,762,728,122), scrollY=0.
768 Healthcare details: component (392,795,118.40625,20), notice (24,762,728,122), scrollY=502.
Each component rectangle is fully contained inside the notice. Nine elementFromPoint samples per component all hit notice descendants, not the focused element. Actual screenshots inspected confirm full visual coverage. Exact geometry matches the worker's four reported targets. The additional 'Plan explanation and comparison' sampled candidate is EXCLUDED: its left edge at x=16 extends beyond notice x=24, so it is partly visible. Point sampling alone is not sufficient to call that a 2.4.11 failure.

The notice is automatic system content, not a disclosure directly opened by this keyboard user. Reaching Keep editing later does not satisfy immediate unobscured focus. W3C explicitly describes completely covering sticky notifications as failures: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-not-obscured-minimum.html .

