Full-site preparation association, not blanket certification
Read exact reports/DI5-a11y-baseline.md; final actual-render audit prepared independently of worker integration scripts. Commands `rtk proxy node baseline.cjs`, `rtk proxy node run-axe.cjs`, `rtk proxy node manual.cjs` and remainder-only `rtk proxy env REMAINING=1 node manual.cjs`, `rtk proxy node responsive.cjs` in final snapshot. All nine nav routes dashboard/explorer/insights/major-expenses/whatif/accounts/transfers/filemanager/duplicates, both themes1440: 18 HTTP200 actual-render captures, zero load failures; npx @axe-core/cli WCAG audit exit0, zero automated violations, 20 incomplete rules/464 node occurrences. Explicit label-name audit zero; 65-step Tab inventory per page/theme. Twelve Dashboard/Insights theme/viewport states at390/768/1440 have no document overflow. These initial-state audits did not trigger the dirty refresh overlay; they do not contradict F1.
All17 point-by-point preparation and limitations are in PREPARATION.md: structure, tables, native controls, label association, validation/form formats, contrast/non-color meaning, focus/HTMX, chart alternatives/themes, signed currency, banners/motion/suppression/dialogs. Prior DI3/DI4/DI6 accepted detailed evidence is associated only for unchanged scoped behavior, not used to excuse the newly demonstrated combined state. Validation writes/destructive actions were not exercised. Baseline input-label gaps and What-If chart-alternative uncertainty remain OBSERVATIONS rather than extra invented failures. Only F1 determines this FAIL.

